# Runtime state. The signing key in particular must never be committed:
# it is what makes a certificate from this installation verifiable. The API
# key file is the credential for api/website.php, the DB config carries a
# database password, the admin password hash gates admin/, and the GitHub
# config holds a personal access token — none of these may ever be committed
# either.
/data/secret.key
/data/api-keys.txt
/data/db-config.php
/data/admin-password.php
/data/github-config.php
/data/rate/
/data/inflight.txt

# Local scratch
*.log
/tmp/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Nothing here uses Composer or npm, and adding them is a design change,
# not a convenience. These entries exist so an accidental install is caught.
/vendor/
/node_modules/
composer.lock
package-lock.json
